  "annotations": [
    {
      "severity": "major",
      "description": "Targeting the opponent with 'draw 3, lose 3 life' gives the opponent massive card advantage (3 cards) for a trivial 3 damage when they're at 20 life. The UR spells opponent will use those cards to find answers and counterspells. Haiku Hype's hand is full of redundant Requiting Hexes with no targets and an uncastable Doomsday Excruciator - they desperately need to draw cards themselves.",
      "action_taken": "Selected mode 2 of Insatiable Avarice intending to target the opponent, giving them 3 cards for 3 damage.",
      "better_line": "Target yourself with mode 2 to draw 3 cards and lose 3 life (going to 15 life), finding action to close the game with Harvester of Misery on board. Alternatively, use both modes to tutor a key card to the top and then draw it plus 2 more.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 72,
      "player": "Haiku Hype",
      "decision_index": 73,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Chose the tutor mode of Insatiable Avarice (put a card on top of library) instead of the draw-3 mode. The tutor delays the card by a turn, while drawing 3 cards immediately for {B}{B}{B} would provide much more card advantage. With a hand full of narrow removal (3x Requiting Hex) and expensive cards they can't cast yet, raw card draw to find playable action seems superior to a delayed tutor.",
      "action_taken": "Selected only the tutor mode (+{2}) of Insatiable Avarice, paying {2}{B} to search for a card and put it on top of library.",
      "better_line": "Select the draw-3 mode (+{B}{B}) instead, paying {B}{B}{B} total to draw three cards and lose 3 life, providing immediate card advantage to find relevant spells.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 72,
      "player": "Haiku Hype",
      "decision_index": 73,
    },
    {
      "severity": "major",
      "description": "Targeting the opponent with Insatiable Avarice's draw-three mode gives Qwen3 ESPN 3 cards (massive card advantage) in exchange for only 3 damage. The opponent is at 20 life, so 3 damage is negligible, while giving a UR spells deck 3 extra cards is devastating. The opponent's graveyard is full of counterspells and card draw, and more cards means more interaction to deal with Haiku Hype's threats.",
      "action_taken": "Targeted Qwen3 ESPN with Insatiable Avarice's draw-three mode, giving the opponent 3 cards and dealing 3 damage.",
      "better_line": "Target yourself (Haiku Hype) with the draw-three mode to draw 3 cards and lose 3 life. At 18 life, going to 15 is fine, and drawing 3 cards would help find lands or additional interaction to press the advantage with the Harvester of Misery on board.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 72,
      "player": "Haiku Hype",
      "decision_index": 73,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Qwen3 ESPN has a devastating two-creature combo available: Eddymurk Crab costs just UU (8 instants/sorceries in graveyard) and Sunderflock costs just UU (reduced by Crab's MV 7). Together for 4 mana, Sunderflock bounces all non-Elemental creatures including Harvester of Misery, deploying 10 power. With 6 lands, casting both leaves 2 mana for Spell Pierce backup. Casting Sleight of Hand first uses 1 mana, meaning after the cantrip they can still cast both creatures but lose the ability to hold up Spell Pierce.",
      "action_taken": "Cast Sleight of Hand before deploying Eddymurk Crab + Sunderflock",
      "better_line": "Cast Eddymurk Crab (UU) tapping Harvester of Misery, then cast Sunderflock (UU) bouncing Harvester, hold up Spell Pierce (U) with remaining 2 mana for protection",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 81,
      "player": "Qwen3 ESPN",
      "decision_index": 84,
    },
    {
      "severity": "questionable",
      "description": "Using Spell Pierce on a low-impact cantrip (Sleight of Hand) when Qwen3 ESPN is about to deploy major threats like Eddymurk Crab (which costs only UU with 8 instants/sorceries in graveyard) or Sunderflock. Spell Pierce would be much more valuable protecting these threats from removal spells like Archenemy's Charm or other answers.",
      "action_taken": "Cast Spell Pierce targeting Sleight of Hand",
      "better_line": "Let Sleight of Hand resolve and save Spell Pierce to protect Eddymurk Crab or Sunderflock from removal when deploying them. The opponent denying one card of selection is much less impactful than potentially losing counter protection for a game-winning threat.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 82,
      "player": "Qwen3 ESPN",
      "decision_index": 87,
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "Eddymurk Crab costs only UU with 10 instants/sorceries in graveyard, provides a 5/5 body, taps opponent's creatures, and critically enables Sunderflock next turn (reducing its cost by 7 as an Elemental) to bounce all non-Elemental creatures. Glacial Dragonhunt is just card filtering.",
      "action_taken": "Cast Glacial Dragonhunt instead of Eddymurk Crab",
      "better_line": "Cast Eddymurk Crab for UU, tap Harvester of Misery, then next turn cast Sunderflock for UU to bounce all non-Elemental creatures",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 83,
      "player": "Qwen3 ESPN",
      "decision_index": 88,
    },
    {
      "severity": "major",
      "description": "Chose 'Exile target creature or planeswalker' mode on Archenemy's Charm when the opponent has zero creatures or planeswalkers on the battlefield. The only possible target is their own Harvester of Misery, or the spell fizzles with no legal target. This wastes a powerful BBB spell entirely.",
      "action_taken": "Selected mode 1 (Exile target creature or planeswalker) with no opposing creatures/planeswalkers on board.",
      "better_line": "Choose mode 3 (Put two +1/+1 counters on Harvester of Misery, giving it lifelink) to make it a 7/6 lifelink menace attacker, threatening 7 damage and gaining 7 life. Alternatively, mode 2 to return Doomsday Excruciator from graveyard to hand for future value.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 88,
      "player": "Haiku Hype",
      "decision_index": 93,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "With Winternight Stories, the player is discarding 2 non-creature cards instead of discarding 1 creature card (a duplicate Sunderflock). This wastes an extra card for no benefit. They have 2 Sunderflock in hand and only need 1 for the Eddymurk Crab + Sunderflock combo to bounce the opponent's Doomsday Excruciator.",
      "action_taken": "Chose to discard 2 non-creature cards from Winternight Stories resolution",
      "better_line": "Discard one Sunderflock as a creature card to satisfy Winternight Stories' alternative cost, keeping an extra card in hand (likely a land drop or spell)",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 98,
      "player": "Qwen3 ESPN",
      "decision_index": 112,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "With 11 power of evasive attackers (6/6 flying + 5/4 menace) against an opponent at 7 life with nearly all lands tapped, lethal was already on board. Choosing Mode 2 targeting the opponent gives them 3 cards unnecessarily, which could include bounce spells or other interaction. While the 3 life loss is nice insurance, giving 3 cards to a desperate opponent is an unnecessary risk.",
      "action_taken": "Chose Mode 2 (target player draws 3 cards and loses 3 life) targeting the opponent, giving them 3 cards while having lethal on board.",
      "better_line": "Choose Mode 1 (search library for a card, put on top) to tutor for insurance without giving the opponent any cards, then attack for lethal with the 11 power of evasive creatures against 7 life.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 105,
      "player": "Haiku Hype",
      "decision_index": 117,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Haiku Hype cast Insatiable Avarice choosing only the tutor mode when they have lethal on board with Doomsday Excruciator (6/6 flying) + Harvester of Misery (5/4 menace) = 11 damage against opponent at 7 life with no creatures and all lands tapped. The tutor is unnecessary and wasteful. Additionally, they could have added the draw-three mode targeting the opponent to deal 3 life loss for extra insurance.",
      "action_taken": "Cast Insatiable Avarice with only the tutor mode (search library, put card on top) before attacking with lethal on board.",
      "better_line": "Skip the Insatiable Avarice entirely and just attack with both creatures for lethal (11 damage vs 7 life). If wanting to cast it for some reason, at least add the +{B}{B} mode targeting the opponent to deal 3 life loss.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 105,
      "player": "Haiku Hype",
      "decision_index": 117,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Targeting the opponent with Insatiable Avarice's draw-3-lose-3 mode gives the opponent 3 cards unnecessarily. Haiku Hype already has lethal on board (6/6 flying + 5/4 menace = 11 damage vs 7 life, no blockers, opponent tapped out). The 3 life loss on the opponent is irrelevant since lethal is already guaranteed, but giving them 3 extra cards is pure downside if anything goes wrong.",
      "action_taken": "Targeted Qwen3 ESPN with Insatiable Avarice's draw-3-lose-3 mode, giving the opponent 3 cards while reducing them to 4 life.",
      "better_line": "Target yourself with the draw-3-lose-3 mode to draw 3 cards for insurance (going to 13 life), then attack for lethal. Alternatively, could have just skipped casting Insatiable Avarice entirely and attacked for lethal immediately.",
      "type": "blunder",
